Since the cannonball is still in the air and hasn't hit anything by the fourth frame, and the game stops before impact, we must extrapolate. The cannonball will continue its arc and will hit the robots. The trajectory suggests it will hit robot 1 first (the lowest one under the tall frame), then robot 2 (the one above it), then robot 3 (the lowest one under the short frame), and finally robot 4 (the one above it). The cannonball will knock them down in sequence. The robots are small and yellow, and the cannonball is heavy and fast, so it will destroy them all. After the cannonball hits and the robots fall, they will break the wooden structures. The wooden structures will collapse, but since the robots are already destroyed, they won't be affected by the collapse. The robots are destroyed by the cannonball's impact, not by falling. The game is over when everything has come to rest, and all robots are destroyed.

